To build a strong programming foundation, it is essential to understand the basic computer hardware components, including input and output devices, the CPU, various memory types, and the Operating System.

Input Devices
Input devices are hardware components used to send data and instructions to a computer system. Some common input devices include:

Keyboard: Used to type text and commands into the computer.
Mouse: Allows you to move the cursor and select items on the screen.
Touchpad: Similar to a mouse, used mainly on laptops to move the cursor.
Scanner: Converts physical documents into digital files.
Microphone: Captures audio input for the computer.
Output Devices
Output devices are hardware components that display or produce the results generated by a computer. Common output devices include:

Display Screen (Monitor): Displays visual output such as text, images, and videos.
Speakers: Produce audio output from the computer.
Earphones: Provide audio output and may also include a built-in microphone for input.
Printer: Produces hard copies of digital documents.
